// Edge Recipes (decision 41, docs/edge_recipes.md 4): one binary, one OFX effect per recipe, grouping "Edge
// Recipes". Each recipe has its OWN factory type RecipeFactory<Tag>: the Support library keeps the plugin uid in a
// static member per factory TYPE (ofxsImageEffect.h:204-220), so sharing one class would dispatch every effect to
// the last one constructed (test: recipes_mutant). Pattern verified in Flame by ofx/recipes/probe.
// Hair Locks (WP7): render() runs the recipe's planner (ofx/recipes/core hair_locks.h): Jump Repair (Advanced,
// off) -> region weight -> candidates (Edge Model = ViTMatte through this bundle's mr_ml_runner, Rebuild Detail =
// the strand tracer, which CREATES matte from the picture, the optional Detail clip) -> [strand presence vote:
// WP6 slot, skipped] -> fusion in the Focus Region -> Snap in the region -> Temporal outside the region. Controls
// -> core params, Plan texts and view colours: hair_locks_ui.h; the candidate adapters: hair_locks_sources.h.
// Nothing enabled (or every step skipped): the Source alpha bit for bit (2.4). The model step is gated per step
// (4.6: gate.h checkGate + the selected model installed); the classical steps always run.
// Inputs (4.4, decisions 4/35): Source = picture + base matte on its alpha; optional masks Detail, FocusRegion
// (declared as Matte Merge's, plugin_merge.cpp). Colour as Matte Refine ML (decisions 23, 34: Picture Colour
// Auto / Bypass through the preferred-colourspace request).
// Footers: Flame did not show a persistent message as a footer in the probe; the Plan label strings (rewritten per
// render) carry the same information in <= 28 characters; the persistent message is still set (as plugin 2).
// Log: the shared log; every line of this bundle carries the node "recipes:<recipe>:<id>" (the process-wide
// component stays "ofx": setLogComponent would rename every plugin's lines in the Flame process, log.h).

